WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.002 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This was obviously
an incredibly close cast.

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:03.336 align:start size:94% position:6%
You guys got along very well
yes?

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:04.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-Is that safe to say?

00:00:04.404 --> 00:00:05.405 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Is it nice to kind of --

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:06.806 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, obviously, you hav
a premiere,

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:08.174 align:start size:94% position:6%
you do a little bit of
press together.

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:09.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is it nice to see everybod
again?

00:00:09.409 --> 00:00:10.010 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-It's so nice.

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:11.544
I mean, you know, we've all kept
in touch

00:00:11.544 --> 00:00:14.647
since we finished the film
and it kind of doesn't feel like

00:00:14.647 --> 00:00:16.149 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's been a year
since we finished.

00:00:16.149 --> 00:00:20.453 size:81% position:41%
But we've all gone off
and done other things.

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:22.255 align:start size:94% position:6%
Emma's been sort of
saving the world.

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:24.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Flo has been really busy
working,

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:25.158 size:88% position:44% line:92%
and Eliza's on Broadway.

00:00:25.158 --> 00:00:27.027 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you've been
Christmas shopping.

00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:28.094 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I've been --
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:30.063
I've been on Amazon, just
getting my little gifts.

00:00:30.063 --> 00:00:33.199
You know, decorating the tree.
So we're all serving society

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:36.903
-Everybody's kind of evenl
successful for the past -- yeah.

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:37.737 line:92%
-Yeah, I feel -- I feel so

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:43.376
And Meryl's, you know -- but
yeah, we all get on really well,

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:45.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's just been so nice
to get back together.

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:46.946 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You had a couple of roommates
in the cast, right?

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:47.614 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Florence and Eliza.

00:00:47.614 --> 00:00:50.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
You guys, you basically
lived together

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:51.317 line:92%
over the course of the shooting?

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:53.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, we lived in this little
sort of complex

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:56.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
in a place called Bedford
in Massachusetts.

00:00:56.723 --> 00:00:59.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we were the old--
or we were the youngest people

00:00:59.626 --> 00:01:02.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
probably by about like 30 year
I would say.

00:01:02.262 --> 00:01:06.399 size:75% position:38%
Everyone was very --
was very old there.

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:06.933 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:11.104
Which I prefer being aroun
much, much older people,

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:13.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
or very, very young people
so it was nice.

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:15.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
We sort of bonded
because of that.

00:01:15.175 --> 00:01:16.209 line:92%
We only really had each other.

00:01:16.209 --> 00:01:18.645 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Were the old people
happy to have you around?

00:01:18.645 --> 00:01:20.513 line:92%
Were they as happy to have you

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:20.947 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
No. Yeah.

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:22.582 size:81% position:41%
-But I mean, we're not
like mads, you know?

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:24.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're not like
some 20-year-olds

00:01:24.217 --> 00:01:27.454
where we're out all night,
playing music, you know.

00:01:27.454 --> 00:01:27.987 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:29.856 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm not, as you can tell
by my finger guns.

00:01:29.856 --> 00:01:32.158 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The very way you did that
yeah.

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:32.659 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.659 --> 00:01:35.428
Even if you had said, "We're the
kind of people that play music,"

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:37.630 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would have been like,
"No, you're not."

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:38.998 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-You're really not.

00:01:38.998 --> 00:01:42.168
-You've given yourself away with
your light finger gunning.

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:45.605 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I play a bit of Stevie Nicks.
You know?

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:46.406 line:92%
-See, that's right in the --

00:01:46.406 --> 00:01:48.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, Stevie Nicks
is the wheelhouse of the peopl

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:49.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
that were living in
that complex.

00:01:49.309 --> 00:01:51.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
They should have been thrilled
to have you around.

00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:52.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I think
they would have been.

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:56.583
Maybe if it was just me, but
maybe Eliza and Florence sort --

00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:57.484 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-They spooked them.

00:01:57.484 --> 00:01:58.418 line:92%
-They sabotaged any chance

00:01:58.418 --> 00:02:01.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had of becoming friends
with these people.

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:03.423 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, exactly.

00:02:03.423 --> 00:02:05.291 line:92%
We talked -- when Timothee

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:07.327 align:start size:94% position:6%
your co-star Timothee Chalamet
was here,

00:02:07.327 --> 00:02:08.394 line:92%
he talked about dance lessons,

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:10.630 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause there's dancing
in the film.

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:11.064 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:12.332 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And Greta, the fantastic
director of the film,

00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:14.367 size:81% position:41%
gave you guys dance --
Was that fun for you?

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:17.203 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you fashion yourself
much of a dancer?

00:02:17.203 --> 00:02:17.770 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.038 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh, yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:22.575
I don't know why you had to as
me that. It's pretty obvious

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:29.449
I like to think that I'm a great
dancer when I've had a few

00:02:29.449 --> 00:02:30.216 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:34.254
-But, when -- you know,
in the daytime, I come to

00:02:34.254 --> 00:02:37.724
the very sober realization tha
I'm probably not a great dancer.

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:39.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
I kind of look like a muppet
dancing I think.

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:42.896
I'm all -- my friends always say
that I'm all arms.

00:02:42.896 --> 00:02:46.399 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
I'm very sort of, like, bendy.

00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:48.067 align:start size:94% position:6%
Tim is actually
a really good dancer,

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:52.005 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I think he did ballet
for a while as well, so he's -

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:53.439 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-He had a leg up on you.

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:54.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:57.911
-But I was very good at sticking
to the steps, and he would try

00:02:57.911 --> 00:02:59.546 line:92%
and change it and I was like

00:02:59.546 --> 00:03:01.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
"No, no.
Let's follow the rules."

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:02.515 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:02.515 --> 00:03:04.083 line:92%
And we'll have fun within that

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:05.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Structure.

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:06.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, no free styling.
-No.

00:03:06.586 --> 00:03:08.721 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You have a --
There's a traumatic scene

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:11.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
where your character Jo
cuts her hair.

00:03:11.424 --> 00:03:11.858 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:13.259 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then you have to
wear a wig.

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:14.694 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I do.
-And this is lovely.

00:03:14.694 --> 00:03:17.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
One of your co-stars
helped you --

00:03:17.063 --> 00:03:17.630 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-We named her.

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:19.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You named the wig?
-We named the wig.

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:22.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, and what was
the wig's name?

00:03:22.435 --> 00:03:23.603 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Pam.
-Yeah.

00:03:23.603 --> 00:03:24.504 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.504 --> 00:03:25.371 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Her name was Pam.

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:26.773 line:92%
She was from Perth in Australia.

00:03:26.773 --> 00:03:28.675 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is a terrible
Australian accent.

00:03:28.675 --> 00:03:31.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, my goodness.
-To any Australians, I'm sorry

00:03:31.311 --> 00:03:33.713 size:84% position:42%
-So Pam had a backstory
and, like, an accent?

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:36.482 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. So, like, I have this
other beautiful wig,

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:38.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's very long
and sort of luscious.

00:03:38.785 --> 00:03:40.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this wig
is equally brilliant.

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:43.856
I mean, what we wanted to do -
because, you know, sometimes

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:46.292 align:start size:94% position:6%
when characters --
-This is Pam here?

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:47.093 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's Pam.
-Yeah.

00:03:47.093 --> 00:03:49.996 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's me, and that's Pam
-Yeah, okay. Gotcha.

00:03:49.996 --> 00:03:52.298 align:start size:94% position:6%
Don't make -- Can this --
I'm sorry.

00:03:52.298 --> 00:03:53.066 line:92%
Can this just be about Pam

00:03:53.066 --> 00:03:56.035 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know that's you, but can w
just give her a little --

00:03:56.035 --> 00:03:56.970 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Alright.
-Okay, fine.

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:59.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But I mean you have me
on the show.

00:03:59.339 --> 00:03:59.772 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:03:59.772 --> 00:04:01.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
-In that case,
bring Pam on to the show.

00:04:01.507 --> 00:04:02.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Alright?

00:04:02.175 --> 00:04:04.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We tried to book Pam and we
heard from your people

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:05.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
that she was not allowed
to come on.

00:04:05.945 --> 00:04:08.181
-Wow. Pam's back in Perth
right now, on Trip Advisor

00:04:08.181 --> 00:04:11.484
We had this thing where we wer
like, she's the kind of person

00:04:11.484 --> 00:04:14.354 align:start size:94% position:6%
that would, like, put bad
reviews up online of like B&amp;Bs

00:04:14.354 --> 00:04:17.490
that she had stayed in
and probably like carries around

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:19.759 align:start size:94% position:6%
a clipboard
just for the hell of it.

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:20.460 line:92%
Like, she's one of those.

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:23.429 align:start size:94% position:6%
-She's a very like, sort o
a vicious wig, it sounds like.

00:04:23.429 --> 00:04:26.466 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, she's just got
a lot of opinions. You know?

00:04:26.466 --> 00:04:27.333 line:92%
-You're very good with accents

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:29.969
Did people tell you you ha
a bad Australian accent?

00:04:29.969 --> 00:04:30.903 line:92%
-Eliza tells me all the time

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:32.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I've got
a bad Australian accent,

00:04:32.839 --> 00:04:33.673 line:92%
and Margot Robbie tells me

00:04:33.673 --> 00:04:35.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I've got
a bad Australian accent.

00:04:35.341 --> 00:04:36.442 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Can we hear it again
real quick?

00:04:36.442 --> 00:04:39.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Australian accent ] I mean,
what do you want me to say

00:04:39.479 --> 00:04:40.113 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You know, I'm Pam.

00:04:40.113 --> 00:04:44.050 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm Pam,
and I'm here to entertain.

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:45.151 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:45.151 --> 00:04:47.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's pretty good.
It's pretty good.

00:04:47.754 --> 00:04:48.888 line:92%
-[ Normal voice ] It's not

00:04:48.888 --> 00:04:50.990 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank God Eliza is on stag
right now.

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:53.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
Otherwise she would be
so embarrassed.

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:54.193 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Thank you.

00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:55.862 align:start size:94% position:6%
Please do give
all of our best to Pam.

00:04:55.862 --> 00:04:58.798
-I will. She was asking for you,
all of you.

00:04:58.798 --> 00:04:59.365 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-All of us.

00:04:59.365 --> 00:05:01.834
-She really wants everyone
to go see "Little Women."

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:03.469 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's great.
-On Christmas Day.

00:05:03.469 --> 00:05:05.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thanks so much for being here
-Thanks, Seth.

00:05:05.872 --> 00:05:09.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's always such a lovely -
lovely to have you here.

00:05:09.309 --> 00:05:10.843 line:92%
Saoirse Ronan, everybody.

